WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.129
And we're in the final minute
of added time.

2
00:00:05.549 --> 00:00:09.261
AFC Richmond and Nottingham Forest are
level with two goals apiece.

3
00:00:10.387 --> 00:00:15.225
Obisanya switches play.
He finds Rojas, who has room.

4
00:00:15.308 --> 00:00:16.308
Oh!

5
00:00:19.563 --> 00:00:20.772
And it's a penalty!

6
00:00:22.107 --> 00:00:25.819
A giant opportunity for the Greyhounds
to change their club's tide here.

7
00:00:25.902 --> 00:00:27.153
Nice pass, Sam!

8
00:00:27.696 --> 00:00:28.697
Here we go, Dani!

9
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:29.948
-Yeah! Yes!
-Nice, nice.

10
00:00:30.031 --> 00:00:34.077
Huge relief for Colin Hughes after
he was liable for Forest's equalizer.

11
00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:38.456
Richmond has started the season
with seven straight ties…

12
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.792
and if this match ends in a draw,
they will tie the record,

13
00:00:40.875 --> 00:00:44.629
which is currently
a tie between Southampton and Swansea.

14
00:00:44.713 --> 00:00:45.881
Chris, can you even imagine

15
00:00:45.964 --> 00:00:48.633
starting a season
with seven consecutive draws?

16
00:00:48.717 --> 00:00:50.176
I sure can, Arlo.

17
00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:53.263
And that's because I'm a right-brained
dominant with a knack for make-believe.

18
00:00:55.056 --> 00:00:56.683
Is it okay if I pray?

19
00:00:56.766 --> 00:00:59.686
Yeah, of course. But to which god
and in what language, you know?

20
00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:01.187
You could cross your fingers, make a wish.

21
00:01:01.271 --> 00:01:02.272
There you go.

22
00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:06.860
The Richmond faithful,
who've recently gone through so much,

23
00:01:06.943 --> 00:01:09.237
still fervently behind their club.

24
00:01:10.196 --> 00:01:11.197
Keep on him.

25
00:01:14.075 --> 00:01:15.285
Go on. Yeah!

26
00:01:17.412 --> 00:01:19.581
And a hush falls over Nelson Road…

27
00:01:23.084 --> 00:01:25.212
With the exception of
Richmond's venerable mascot,

28
00:01:25.295 --> 00:01:28.340
Earl Greyhound, howling his encouragement.

29
00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:36.348
Will Dani Rojas deliver the good boy
their first win of the season?

30
00:01:36.431 --> 00:01:37.557
Please, please, please, please.

31
00:01:37.641 --> 00:01:38.808
Come on, Dani.

32
00:01:41.603 --> 00:01:43.146
Football is life.

33
00:02:15.428 --> 00:02:17.264
-Oh, no.
-Oh, my God.

34
00:02:17.347 --> 00:02:19.266
I promise that's not what I wished for.

35
00:02:44.082 --> 00:02:46.835
That poor creature. It's so tragic.

36
00:02:46.918 --> 00:02:48.128
Awful turn of events.

37
00:02:48.211 --> 00:02:50.380
You don't think that people will hate us
because of it, do you?

38
00:02:50.463 --> 00:02:51.882
Well, it was obviously
a horrible accident,

39
00:02:51.965 --> 00:02:54.134
but I guess that one perk of being
in a lower division now

40
00:02:54.217 --> 00:02:56.511
is that not every game is televised.

41
00:02:56.595 --> 00:02:58.471
Yes, but, Higgins, the Internet.

42
00:02:58.972 --> 00:03:00.765
Oh, right, the goddamn Internet.

43
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.059
Twitter is going bonkers. Look.

44
00:03:04.102 --> 00:03:06.855
Oh, God. Did we really make
Michael Jordan cry?

45
00:03:06.938 --> 00:03:08.648
-Did you write a statement for Ted?
-Yeah, I did.

46
00:03:08.732 --> 00:03:12.485
But then he said, "Now, don't you fret,
Boba Fett." He's got it covered.

47
00:03:12.569 --> 00:03:13.570
Okay.

48
00:03:14.529 --> 00:03:16.281
-Coach!
-All right, Marcus,

49
00:03:16.364 --> 00:03:17.741
-what do you got for me?
-Coach Lasso,

50
00:03:17.824 --> 00:03:20.035
how are you feeling about
the team's efforts today?

51
00:03:20.118 --> 00:03:22.579
Well, I feel like everyone played
their hearts out, especially Sam.

52
00:03:22.662 --> 00:03:23.872
Just gets better and better every game.

53
00:03:23.955 --> 00:03:27.000
He's really helping us fill
that giant Roy Kent void, you know.

54
00:03:27.083 --> 00:03:29.044
And how many more matches you think
can end in a draw

55
00:03:29.127 --> 00:03:30.295
before you hit the panic button?

56
00:03:30.378 --> 00:03:33.340
Well, Marcus, there's two buttons
I never like to hit, all right?

57
00:03:33.423 --> 00:03:34.674
And that's "panic" and "snooze."

58
00:03:34.758 --> 00:03:36.218
Who else?

59
00:03:36.301 --> 00:03:38.011
What about this fella right here?

60
00:03:38.678 --> 00:03:41.431
-Trent Crimm--
-The Independent.

61
00:03:42.307 --> 00:03:46.478
I was wondering if you had any comments
on Earl, the dog Dani Rojas killed today.

62
00:03:48.813 --> 00:03:51.066
Trent Crimm, bringing that heat.

63
00:03:55.946 --> 00:03:56.947
Yeah.

64
00:03:58.782 --> 00:04:01.826
Well, when I was three years old,
I got attacked by our neighbor's dog.

65
00:04:02.369 --> 00:04:04.955
I-I don't remember it happening,
but my mother said it was pretty--

66
00:04:05.038 --> 00:04:06.248
pretty scary, you know.

67
00:04:07.415 --> 00:04:10.168
I do remember being afraid of dogs
while growing up though.

68
00:04:10.252 --> 00:04:12.712
Like if I was at a friend's house
for a sleepover or something,

69
00:04:12.796 --> 00:04:16.216
they'd have to keep their family dog
outside, otherwise I'd bawl my eyes out.

70
00:04:18.759 --> 00:04:22.764
Then in high school, our neighbor,
Mr. Grady, well, his wife passed away.

71
00:04:23.765 --> 00:04:25.976
And he was real sad about that,
as you can imagine,

72
00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:29.563
and he just kinda stopped
taking care of their dog.

73
00:04:30.772 --> 00:04:32.941
Same one that bit me. His name was Hank.

74
00:04:36.444 --> 00:04:38.613
And so I started looking after him,
you know.

75
00:04:38.697 --> 00:04:41.616
Feeding him, taking him on walks,
playing fetch, all that fun stuff.

76
00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:45.370
Eventually, Mr. Grady's son moved
his dad into a nursing home,

77
00:04:45.453 --> 00:04:48.290
and he asked if I wanted to keep Hank,
and I was like, "Yeah. Heck, yeah."

78
00:04:49.666 --> 00:04:52.335
And then a year or so after that
we had to put Hank to sleep.

79
00:04:55.463 --> 00:04:57.632
It's funny to think about
the things in your life…

80
00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:02.220
that can make you cry just knowing
that they existed,

81
00:05:02.304 --> 00:05:04.097
can then become
the same thing that make you cry

82
00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:05.724
knowing that they're now gone.

83
00:05:11.062 --> 00:05:12.898
I think those things come into our lives…

84
00:05:14.274 --> 00:05:16.234
to help us get from one place
to a better one.

85
00:05:19.988 --> 00:05:22.324
And I hope we helped Earl do just that.

86
00:05:23.617 --> 00:05:25.827
We gonna miss him around here
a whole bunch. Yeah.

87
00:05:31.791 --> 00:05:33.126
And how's Dani doing?

88
00:05:33.835 --> 00:05:34.836
I haven't spoken with him yet,

89
00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:37.505
but I just hope he's not being
too hard on himself, you know.

90
00:05:40.383 --> 00:05:42.219
He's been like this for 20 minutes.

91
00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:47.182
He's gonna use all the hot water.

92
00:05:48.391 --> 00:05:49.601
-Yeah.
-Yeah, you're right.

93
00:06:01.655 --> 00:06:03.698
Hey, Dani. What ya doing?

94
00:06:04.699 --> 00:06:06.326
Washing the death off of me.

95
00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:16.586
Well, I-- I recommend
you use a little soap.

96
00:06:17.212 --> 00:06:20.590
Helps get the eternal rest out of those
tough-to-reach places, you know.

97
00:06:20.674 --> 00:06:21.925
Gracias, Coach.

98
00:06:23.301 --> 00:06:26.471
Well, hey, don't forget,
football is life, right?

99
00:06:29.182 --> 00:06:30.892
I know. It used to be.

100
00:06:36.147 --> 00:06:37.148
I got nothing.

101
00:06:45.031 --> 00:06:46.658
Okay, so, fellas,

102
00:06:46.741 --> 00:06:49.327
let's go ahead and give Dani
a little bit of space right now, yeah?

103
00:06:49.411 --> 00:06:50.996
Y'all don't mind showering at home, do ya?

104
00:06:51.079 --> 00:06:52.706
Coach, if it's okay with you,

105
00:06:52.789 --> 00:06:54.583
some of us prefer
to take long baths at home.

106
00:06:54.666 --> 00:06:56.585
Yeah, yeah.

107
00:06:56.668 --> 00:06:58.295
Oh. Yeah, no, okay, that'll work too.

108
00:06:58.378 --> 00:07:00.714
Oh, and hey, way to play out there today.

109
00:07:00.797 --> 00:07:02.424
Y'all kicked their butts
from soup to nuts.

110
00:07:02.507 --> 00:07:03.925
Don't worry, we gonna get a W soon.

111
00:07:04.759 --> 00:07:06.219
We'll see you goldfish on Monday.

112
00:07:06.887 --> 00:07:07.888
Goldfish?

113
00:07:07.971 --> 00:07:11.057
Oh, it means to forget our mistakes
and failures and just move on.

114
00:07:11.766 --> 00:07:14.603
But I didn't make any mistakes.
Only you played poorly.

115
00:07:17.355 --> 00:07:19.691
Hey, guys, Jan Maas is not being rude.

116
00:07:19.774 --> 00:07:20.775
He's just being Dutch.

117
00:07:22.652 --> 00:07:23.945
-Yeah, yeah.
-True.

118
00:07:31.578 --> 00:07:33.747
I'm telling you,
all these ties are my fault.

119
00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:36.666
It's straight up celestial payback
for the Man City game.

120
00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:39.669
There I was wishing and hoping
for a freaking tie,

121
00:07:39.753 --> 00:07:41.338
and now the karma police are making good

122
00:07:41.421 --> 00:07:43.590
on showing me what I get
when I mess with them.

123
00:07:43.673 --> 00:07:45.967
The team's playing well, Ted,
just a little unlucky, that's all.

124
00:07:46.051 --> 00:07:49.346
"Unlucky." Yeah. Man, I love the way
y'all use that word over here.

125
00:07:49.429 --> 00:07:51.848
Back home, if a team was playing poorly,
we don't call 'em unlucky.

126
00:07:51.932 --> 00:07:53.975
-What do we call 'em, Coach?
-New York Jets.

127
00:07:54.059 --> 00:07:55.685
-There it is.
-Hey, Coach.

128
00:07:55.769 --> 00:07:58.021
Sorry to interrupt.
Can I leave a little early today?

129
00:07:58.104 --> 00:08:00.523
But part of your job is to stay
until the whole team's gone.

130
00:08:00.607 --> 00:08:03.485
No, yes, of course. It's just,
it's my mum's 50th birthday--

131
00:08:03.568 --> 00:08:04.986
Oh. Oh.

132
00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:07.197
And what position does your mum play
on the team again?

133
00:08:08.573 --> 00:08:11.368
It's okay, Will. Tell your mom
a happy birthday from all of us,

134
00:08:11.451 --> 00:08:13.662
and if she ever wants to try out
for the team, she's more than welcome.

135
00:08:13.745 --> 00:08:14.955
Lovely.

136
00:08:21.086 --> 00:08:22.337
You gotta stay on 'em.

137
00:08:23.129 --> 00:08:24.798
Pressure makes pearls, right?

138
00:08:26.258 --> 00:08:27.384
Wait, that's wrong.

139
00:08:27.467 --> 00:08:29.928
It's diamonds-- Shit! I messed it up.

140
00:08:30.011 --> 00:08:31.555
No, you didn't mess it up.
You were just--

141
00:08:31.638 --> 00:08:33.139
-Unlucky.
-Yes!

142
00:08:36.726 --> 00:08:37.936
Thanks.

143
00:08:38.562 --> 00:08:39.688
That's odd.

144
00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:43.608
We just received a giant food delivery
from our rivals over at Brentford F.C.

145
00:08:43.692 --> 00:08:45.235
That's nice. What kind of food?

146
00:08:45.318 --> 00:08:46.319
Thai.

147
00:08:46.903 --> 00:08:48.321
Oh, now I get it.

148
00:08:49.739 --> 00:08:51.825
-Howdy, y'all.
-Ted!

149
00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:54.703
What do you say to a cocktail,
Coach Lasso?

150
00:08:54.786 --> 00:08:56.454
Oh, the same thing I'd say to Diane Sawyer

151
00:08:56.538 --> 00:08:58.456
if she ever asked me out on a date:
"Yes, please."

152
00:08:59.207 --> 00:09:02.419
Boy, oh, boy, oh, boy, oh, boy.

153
00:09:03.044 --> 00:09:04.004
How you feeling?

154
00:09:04.087 --> 00:09:05.839
Well, Keeley, I feel like

155
00:09:05.922 --> 00:09:08.258
a bigger loser than
the biggest loser from The Biggest Loser.

156
00:09:08.842 --> 00:09:10.802
Oh, look on the bright side, Ted.

157
00:09:10.886 --> 00:09:13.054
We are still undefeated.

158
00:09:13.138 --> 00:09:14.598
Okay, sure. Thank you.

159
00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:16.141
How's Dani doing?

160
00:09:17.475 --> 00:09:19.102
Oh, he's a little shell-shocked,

161
00:09:19.185 --> 00:09:21.146
but Dani's a lot like
an expensive tape measure.

162
00:09:21.229 --> 00:09:23.356
-He snaps back real quick.
-Yeah.

163
00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:24.858
What about Earl's owner?
He doing all right?

164
00:09:24.941 --> 00:09:26.902
-Yeah, fortunately he is.
-Oh, good.

165
00:09:26.985 --> 00:09:29.613
Yes, and you're now looking at
the very new, very generous,

166
00:09:29.696 --> 00:09:33.867
very guilt-riddled benefactor
of Richmond's largest dog shelter.

167
00:09:34.367 --> 00:09:35.577
Barkingham Palace.

168
00:09:36.661 --> 00:09:37.913
It's a good name.

169
00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:40.332
-To Earl.
-To Earl.

170
00:09:40.415 --> 00:09:41.666
To Earl.

171
00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:44.044
Okay, I should go.

172
00:09:44.127 --> 00:09:46.796
I promised the boys we'd watch
Empire Strikes Back tonight,

173
00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:48.590
and I have to get my thoughts together

174
00:09:48.673 --> 00:09:51.051
for when they ask
about Luke and Leia making out.

175
00:09:51.134 --> 00:09:53.178
-Oh, right.
-Wish me luck.

176
00:09:53.261 --> 00:09:54.512
Good luck, Higgins.

177
00:09:54.596 --> 00:09:55.639
Bye, Leslie.

178
00:09:55.722 --> 00:09:58.475
-Hey. May the force be with you.
-And also with you.

179
00:09:58.558 --> 00:09:59.559
All right.

180
00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:02.229
-Oh, my God!
-Oh, is that him?

181
00:10:02.312 --> 00:10:03.855
-Yes, yes, yes.
-Come on! Oh, good!

182
00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:06.191
Okay.

183
00:10:06.274 --> 00:10:07.567
Hey, him who?

184
00:10:08.526 --> 00:10:10.445
-And?
-Well, I mean…

185
00:10:10.528 --> 00:10:12.697
-Okay, but?
-Oh, no. Totally.

186
00:10:12.781 --> 00:10:14.532
-Good, I'm proud of you.
-Thanks.

187
00:10:14.616 --> 00:10:15.909
Am I allowed to speak yet?

188
00:10:16.493 --> 00:10:18.787
Oh, sorry, Ted.
It's just a little bit of girl talk

189
00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:22.290
about a gentleman suitor
I've gone out with a few times.

190
00:10:22.374 --> 00:10:25.126
Nice. A little girl talk. I get it.

191
00:10:25.835 --> 00:10:27.045
What's his name--

192
00:10:30.715 --> 00:10:33.343
Are you guys up for a double date
next week? Let him prove his mettle.

193
00:10:33.426 --> 00:10:36.137
-Abso-fucking-lutely.
-Can you ask Roy if he's free?

194
00:10:36.221 --> 00:10:37.472
-He's free. Don't worry.
-Okay, cool.

195
00:10:37.556 --> 00:10:39.266
Hey, did Roy come to the game today?

196
00:10:39.849 --> 00:10:41.476
Oh, no, he didn't. Sorry, Ted.

197
00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:43.937
Oh, no, that's okay. I'm sure
he'll swing by at some point, right?

198
00:10:44.604 --> 00:10:47.065
Hey, he knows he's always got a ticket
waiting for him at will call, yeah?

199
00:10:47.148 --> 00:10:48.149
-Yeah.
-Good, okay.

200
00:10:48.233 --> 00:10:50.902
And don't forget,
I don't put it under his name.

201
00:10:50.986 --> 00:10:52.946
I don't want folks messing with him.
It's under an alias.

202
00:10:53.029 --> 00:10:56.449
Like, last week it was
Loretta Lynn, this week was Dolly Parton,

203
00:10:56.533 --> 00:10:59.160
and next week is, if I remember correctly,
Shania Twain.

204
00:10:59.244 --> 00:11:00.412
Just brilliant.

205
00:11:00.495 --> 00:11:01.580
And it's nothing personal.

206
00:11:01.663 --> 00:11:03.957
It's just that he's been so busy
with this new coaching gig.

207
00:11:05.292 --> 00:11:06.334
You listen to me!

208
00:11:06.918 --> 00:11:10.380
You play like that next week,
you can kiss the trophy goodbye,

209
00:11:10.463 --> 00:11:14.593
'cause today, you all played like
a bunch of little pricks!

210
00:11:14.676 --> 00:11:15.677
You hear me?

211
00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.387
Yes, Coach!

212
00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:20.432
Except for Kokoruda. Way to put
your body on the line out there.

213
00:11:20.515 --> 00:11:22.434
You know it, Coach.

214
00:11:22.517 --> 00:11:25.353
All right,
Monika's mum brought orange slices.

215
00:11:25.437 --> 00:11:27.439
Don't eat the peels, you animals.
Off you go.

216
00:11:28.064 --> 00:11:30.108
-Keeley!
-Hey, Phoebs!

217
00:11:31.568 --> 00:11:33.987
Coach Kent. They're eight years old.

218
00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:36.698
-You can't call them little pricks.
-Sorry, Ms. Bowen.

219
00:11:36.781 --> 00:11:38.408
Even when they're being little pricks.

220
00:11:38.491 --> 00:11:40.285
See you on Monday at school, girls.

221
00:11:40.368 --> 00:11:41.995
-Bye, Ms. Bowen.
-Hey, babe.

222
00:11:42.078 --> 00:11:43.079
Bye, Ms. Bowen.

223
00:11:44.289 --> 00:11:46.374
-All right, who wants some hot chocolate?
-Me!

224
00:11:46.458 --> 00:11:48.251
-I do.
-Yeah, let's go!

225
00:11:53.131 --> 00:11:54.716
Oh! Before I forget,

226
00:11:54.799 --> 00:11:57.219
Rebecca wanted to see if we could do
some double date action next week.

227
00:11:57.302 --> 00:11:58.678
Fucking hell.

228
00:11:58.762 --> 00:12:02.015
Bad word, Uncle Roy. You owe me one quid.

229
00:12:02.098 --> 00:12:03.266
Put it on my tab.

230
00:12:03.850 --> 00:12:05.393
-Can you hold this, please?
-Course.

231
00:12:05.936 --> 00:12:07.145
Come on. It'll be fun.

232
00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:10.607
-Fine.
-Thank you.

233
00:12:12.734 --> 00:12:14.236
Phoebe, how was the match today?

234
00:12:14.778 --> 00:12:16.363
-Outstanding.
-Yeah?

235
00:12:16.446 --> 00:12:18.949
I got a red card
for elbowing a girl in her neck.

236
00:12:19.658 --> 00:12:20.951
And I'm very proud.

237
00:12:22.202 --> 00:12:23.536
What?

238
00:12:25.121 --> 00:12:28.083
Well, I know that you guys
are just gonna smash it next week.

239
00:12:28.166 --> 00:12:29.542
Me too.

240
00:12:30.502 --> 00:12:31.920
